 "notes": "95% C.L. exclusion contour from Fig. 7, 'Galaxy Cluster magnetic field (conservative)' region (green vector path in fig7.pdf of the e-print), which the paper presents as its robust main result (g_gamma-a < 2.1e-11 GeV^-1 around 25 neV); the alternative 'Intergalactic Magnetic Field (optimistic, 1 nG)' region was not reported. Axes calibrated from major tick marks and verified against the dashed CAST line (reproduces 8.8e-11 GeV^-1). Points trace the closed boundary of the excluded blob along the path (down the low-mass side, across the minimum, up the high-mass side), so mass ordering has a small non-monotonic lean at the start; the contour is truncated at the figure's top edge, g = 1.6e-10 GeV^-1. Extracted minimum g = 2.09e-11 GeV^-1 at m ~ 31 neV, matching the quoted 2.1e-11. Limit does not assume ALP dark matter, so no density rescaling.",
